   THE AGENT JUDGES WHAT IT HAS JUST LIVED THROUGH OR READ (decision D4). Until then, the
   severity of a shock was purely deterministic — a delay, a missed connection, a network
   incident — and an article, which inflicts nothing, was worth zero. The judgement gives its
   weight to what the simulation does not measure.

   ⚠ THE SEVERITY IS THE AGENT'S, AND ITS ALONE (decision D7 of 2026-09-22). The floor
   `max(I_llm, I_det)` was removed: what the agent says here DECIDES how long the memory
   lives, including when it underestimates a forty-five-minute incident. What replaces the
   floor corrects nothing — the gap to the measured fact is logged and alarmed. That is what
   makes this template critical: there is no longer a guard behind it.

   ⚠ THE ANCHORS ARRIVE IN ENGLISH, under the exact label of the `severity` enumeration. They
   travelled in French until 2026-09-22 — the prompt offered `anodin`…`marquant` while the
   schema only accepted `negligible`…`memorable`.

